      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>Can you make your wrists bigger?</h3></summary><p>Only a little. Wrist size is mostly bone and tendon, which do not grow in adults. Forearm training builds the muscles just above the wrist, and gaining body fat adds a small amount, but the wrist bone itself stays the same.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>What size watch fits my wrist?</h3></summary><p>As a rough guide, wrists under 6.5 inches suit cases of about 34–38 mm, 6.5–7.5 inches suit 36–42 mm, and over 7.5 inches suit 40–46 mm. The lugs should not overhang the edges of your wrist.</p></details>
      <details class="tp-faq"><summary><h3>What bracelet size do I need?</h3></summary><p>Add about half an inch (1.3 cm) to your wrist measurement for a snug bracelet, three-quarters of an inch for a comfortable fit, and about an inch (2.5 cm) for a loose fit.</p></details>
  </section>

